What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my @kinds;
for my $m ("first\n", "second") {
    eval { die $m };
    push @kinds, $@ =~ /line \d+/ ? "located" : "plain";
}
say "@kinds";
```

What does this program print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
my $log = '';
for my $n (4, 0, 2) {
    eval { $log .= 12 / $n; 1 } or do { $log .= 'X' };
    $log .= ',';
}
say $log;
```

This program writes five words to a temporary file, one per line, and reads them back. What number does it print?

```perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use feature qw(say);
use File::Temp qw(tempdir);
my $path = tempdir(CLEANUP => 1) . '/words.txt';
open my $out, '>', $path or die "Cannot write $path: $!";
print {$out} "$_\n" for qw(alpha beta gamma delta epsilon);
close $out;
open my $in, '<', $path or die "Cannot read $path: $!";
while (my $word = <$in>) {
    last if $word =~ /^d/;
}
say $.;
```

What number does this program print? (The source file is saved as UTF-8.)

```perl
